  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a downtrend followed by a sudden spike (e.g., Example 2 and 3), the model systematically underestimates the immediate upside, failing to capture momentum driven by positive sentiment spikes.",
    "The model exhibits a strong mean-reversion bias in volatile regimes; when true outcomes show high volatility with sharp peaks followed by rapid declines, the forecast incorrectly predicts a smooth, linear upward drift.",
    "In periods of mixed or fluctuating sentiment (positive and negative values), the model ignores short-term volatility shocks, resulting in forecasts that are too flat compared to the actual jagged price paths.",
    "The 30-day horizon forecast consistently underestimates the maximum peak value when a significant upward spike occurs within the first 5 days of the forecast window.",
    "When sentiment history contains isolated positive spikes (e.g., 1.00 or 0.33) amidst neutral noise, the model fails to weight these events sufficiently, leading to systematic under-forecasting of subsequent price surges."
  ]
}
